# =============================================================================
# PRIVACY-FIRST .gitignore
#
# This project analyses human genetic data. The repository is public.
# The policy is DENY BY DEFAULT: data and results are excluded, and anything
# that becomes public must be un-ignored explicitly after a disclosure review.
#
# A .gitignore file is a safeguard, not a guarantee. It only prevents files
# from being ADDED; it does not remove files that are already tracked, and it
# does not protect against `git add -f`. See docs/privacy_policy.md.
# =============================================================================

# --- Data: everything is excluded; only the explanatory README is tracked ----
data/*
!data/README.md
!data/**/.gitkeep
# Template files carry structure only - no cohort variants, no real values.
!data/reviewed/
data/reviewed/*
!data/reviewed/*.example.csv
!data/reviewed/*.example.json
!data/external/
data/external/*
!data/external/*.example.csv

# --- Results of real-cohort analyses are never tracked -----------------------
results/
logs/

# --- Defence in depth: block by filename pattern anywhere in the tree --------
# These patterns match intermediate files that carry patient-level information.
# Patterns naming a particular laboratory's export files or identifier scheme
# are study-specific, so they belong in the untracked .git/info/exclude of a
# working copy, not here; see docs/privacy_policy.md.
# They are restricted to data file extensions so that source modules with
# similar names (for example src/mefv/patient_builder.py) remain trackable.
*patient*.csv
*patient*.tsv
*patient*.txt
*patient*.json
*variants_long*
*corrections_log*
*qc_punch_list*
*high_allele_burden*
*_identifiable*
mefv_clean_*

# --- Office documents and PDFs almost always originate from the laboratory ---
*.xlsx
*.xls
*.xlsm
*.docx
*.doc
*.pdf

# --- Clinical reports, screenshots and images ---------------------------------
*report*.pdf
*Screenshot*
*screenshot*
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.tif
*.tiff
*.heic

# --- Completed variant-classification forms (assessor-level judgements) ------
*_filled.*
*_completed.*
*acmg_form_assessor_*

# --- Credentials and local configuration -------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
*.key
*.pem
*token*
*secret*
credentials*
config_local.py
study_parameters*.json
!study_parameters.example.json

# --- Git transport files and archives can carry whole histories or data ------
*.bundle
*.patch
*.tgz
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.zip
*.7z
PRIVATE_*

# --- Python -------------------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
env/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# --- Editors and operating systems --------------------------------------------
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
.ipynb_checkpoints/
~$*

# --- Private owner files: never to be committed --------------------------------
# The privacy denylist and the owner's disposition record belong OUTSIDE the
# repository (the tools refuse a path inside it). These patterns are a second
# line of defence in case one is created here by mistake.
*denylist*
owner_disposition*
*.disposition.json
